1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--ear-training","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/ear-training","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/ear-training","sourceHash":"6b84c9a82027b905df250c5a1b05ae47227b453ec8ae58f71f65816a3fa94556","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:52:51.941Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Ear Training","zh":"听音训练"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Ear training is any exercise specifically designed to improve your ability to hear and distinguish the sounds of the target language.","zh":"听音训练是指专门用来提高你听辨目标语言声音能力的任何练习。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Every language has its own set of sounds, and your native language likely doesn't use all of them. Your brain has learned to filter out unfamiliar sounds, so you need to actively retrain your ears to hear them.","zh":"每种语言都有自己的一套声音，而你的母语很可能并不使用其中的所有声音。你的大脑已经学会过滤陌生的声音，因此你需要主动重新训练听觉，才能听出它们。"}},{"id":"common-approaches","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Common Approaches","zh":"常见方法"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Minimal pairs training:</strong> Listening to pairs of words that differ by only one sound (like \"ship\" vs. \"sheep\" in English) and practicing telling them apart. Many languages have sounds that seem identical to non-native ears but are distinct to native speakers. Minimal pairs training builds the ability to hear those distinctions.","zh":"<strong>最小对立体训练：</strong>聆听仅有一个声音不同的成对词语（例如英语中的“ship”和“sheep”），并练习分辨它们。许多语言中都有一些声音，在非母语者听来似乎完全相同，但母语者却能清楚区分。最小对立体训练可以培养你听出这些区别的能力。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Sound study:</strong> Learning about the phonology (sound system) of your target language — what sounds exist, how they're produced, and how they differ from your native language's sounds. Even a brief overview makes a noticeable difference.","zh":"<strong>语音学习：</strong>了解目标语言的音系（声音系统），包括有哪些声音、这些声音如何发出，以及它们与母语声音有何不同。哪怕只是进行简要了解，也会带来明显改善。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Targeted listening:</strong> Focusing specifically on hard-to-hear sounds during your regular immersion. Once you know what to listen for, you start hearing it everywhere.","zh":"<strong>针对性听力练习：</strong>在日常沉浸中，专门留意那些难以听清的声音。一旦知道应该留意什么，你就会开始在各种内容中听到它。"}},{"id":"why-it-matters","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Matters","zh":"为什么这很重要"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Ear training has a dual benefit: it improves your listening comprehension (you can understand more of what people say) and it improves your pronunciation (you can't produce sounds you can't hear).","zh":"听音训练有双重益处：它能提高听力理解能力（让你听懂更多别人说的话），也能改善发音（听不出的声音也无法准确发出）。"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Even small amounts of ear training — 10-15 minutes a few times a week — produce noticeable results. You don't need to dedicate huge amounts of time to it.","zh":"即使每周只进行几次、每次 10–15 分钟的听音训练，也能产生明显效果。你不必为此投入大量时间。"}},{"id":"resources","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Resources","zh":"资源"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Good resources for ear training depend on your specific language. Common recommendations include Fluent Forever's pronunciation trainers, The Mimic Method, language-specific minimal pairs exercises, and the phonology sections of Wikipedia articles about your target language.","zh":"适合听音训练的资源取决于你所学的具体语言。常见推荐包括 Fluent Forever 的发音训练工具、The Mimic Method、针对特定语言的最小对立体练习，以及维基百科中有关目标语言的条目里的音系部分。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?item=30201-ear-training&amp;type=activity\">-&gt; More information and demonstration</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?item=30201-ear-training&amp;type=activity\">-&gt; 更多信息和演示</a>"}},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Light ear training begins in Phase 1 (as part of Sound Study) and becomes more important in Phase 3 when you're focused on building listening ability.","zh":"阶段 1 会开始进行轻量的听音训练（作为语音学习的一部分）；到了阶段 3，当你着重培养听力时，这项训练会变得更加重要。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
